      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Example: accumulate()"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Consider we have a vector of integers,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "vector<int> numbers {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "To compute its sum,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "accumulate (numbers.begin(), numbers.end() , 0);"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, 0 is an int ,so the function will return 0. Let's see a complete example."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "1#include <iostream>\n2#include <numeric>\n3#include <vector>\n4\n5using namespace std;\n6\n7int main(){\n8\n9    vector<int> numbers{1, 2, 3, 4, 5};\n10\n11   // Accumulate from the beginning of the container to the end with the initial value of 0\n12    int sum = accumulate(numbers.begin(), numbers.end(), 0);\n13\n14    cout << \"The sum is \" << sum;\n15}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "The sum is 15"
    },
